## User preferences

- when the user said "read-only로 동작하라 — 파일을 수정하지 말 것" and "파일 수정 금지" -> keep similar repo-review work audit-only and do not drift into edits [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]
- when the user asked for "파일과 실제 소비자 코드를 직접 읽고 근거를 대라. 추측은 추측이라고 명시하라." -> future refactor/security reviews should stay source-trace driven, read the consumer files directly, and label inference vs verified fact [Task 1][Task 3]
- when the user asked for structured review output with explicit sections, preserve that shape instead of giving one blended narrative; the strongest repeated pattern here was defects/design/traps/order [Task 1][Task 3]
- when the user said `샌드박스에서 codex 초기화가 'Operation not permitted'로 실패하면 재시도하지 말고 그 로그를 그대로 보고하라` -> on similar sandbox init failures, report the exact failure text once and stop retrying that path [Task 2][Task 3]
- when the user enumerated attack vectors or contract edges up front, review the negative space of each contract rather than only the happy path [Task 2][Task 3]

## Reusable knowledge

- `packages/api/src/api/chat_stream.py` mixed four concerns even after being split from `chat.py`: config-error SSE, model-hinting, remote A2A proxying, and local A2A serving; the highest-risk contract is `stream_local_reply()` returning `(context_id, async_iterator, state_dict)` with the mutable `state` filled only after stream exhaustion [Task 1]
- `a2a_server.py` drains the iterator first and then reads `serve_state`, while `chat_approval.py` rebuilds the same graph/resume path; any refactor has to preserve SSE framing, interrupt persistence behavior, GeneratorExit cleanup, and the post-stream decision point [Task 1]
- In this environment, `codex --help` and `codex exec --help` can work while `codex exec` still fails at runtime with `failed to initialize in-process app-server client: Operation not permitted (os error 1)`; the presence of the binary is not enough to assume Codex review can run [Task 2]
- In the same sandbox, `zsh` here-doc prompt construction can fail with `can't create temp file for here document: operation not permitted`, so restricted review flows should avoid temp-file-dependent shell patterns [Task 2]
- `packages/api/src/api/main.py` includes only `blocks.router`, which makes `blocks.py` a de facto facade over prompts CRUD/apply, memory-types CRUD, MCP CRUD/discover/rediscover/test-tool, and `/blocks` aggregation rather than a narrow single-purpose module [Task 3]
- `agents/crud_routes.py` and multiple verifier tests import internals from `api.blocks` directly, so a low-risk split must preserve facade re-exports for symbols like `assert_memory_names_exist`, `_tools_meta_from_details`, `rediscover_mcp_server`, `update_mcp_server`, and `test_mcp_tool` [Task 3]
- The stable behavior traps to preserve in `blocks.py` refactors are: memory-types create/delete/name-change 403 sealing with description edits allowed, auth masking on list/get/aggregate, `auth=\"\"` removing auth, rediscover preserving approval metadata and intersecting enabled tools, 409 guards on active references, non-custom `published=true` returning 400, immutable `source`, and block-version writes on prompt/MCP edits and rediscover [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: a Codex-based review never starts even though the CLI exists. Cause: sandbox blocks in-process app-server initialization. Fix: treat `Operation not permitted` at init as a hard stop for `codex exec`, preserve the exact log, and switch to shell-only evidence gathering if the task still needs analysis [Task 2][Task 3]
- Symptom: prompt preparation fails before the review starts. Cause: a restricted `zsh` session could not create the temp file for a here-doc. Fix: avoid here-doc prompt construction when the sandbox disallows temp-file creation [Task 2]
- Symptom: a refactor proposal breaks consumers/tests immediately after file moves. Cause: the current module is acting as a package facade and its internals are imported directly. Fix: extract helpers behind preserved re-exports first, then split route families gradually [Task 3]
- Symptom: a split plan becomes too abstract and loses the real contracts. Cause: recommendations were derived from file shape alone instead of consumer/test behavior. Fix: inspect direct imports and verifier files before recommending any module boundary [Task 1][Task 3]

